cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use IsoGen, please cite the primary IsoGen paper and the relevant
  method references listed in this file.
title: IsoGen
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Marty
    given-names: Michael T.
    email: mtmarty@utexas.edu
abstract: >-
  Fast isotope-distribution calculations for proteins, nucleic acids, and
  elemental formulas using FFT, BRAIN, and neural-network methods.
version: "1.0.5"
repository-code: "https://github.com/michaelmarty/IsoGen"
url: "https://michaelmarty.github.io/IsoGen/"
license: BSD-3-Clause
keywords:
  - isotope distribution
  - mass spectrometry
  - proteomics
  - protein
  - DNA
  - RNA
  - elemental formula

